{
  "an11.10:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 11.10 ",
  "an11.10:0.2": "1. Dependence ",
  "an11.10:0.3": "At the Peacocks’ Feeding Ground ",
  "an11.10:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Rājagaha, at the monastery for the wanderers in the peacocks’ feeding ground. ",
  "an11.10:1.2": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants, ",
  "an11.10:1.3": "“Mendicants!” ",
  "an11.10:1.4": "“Venerable sir,” they replied. ",
  "an11.10:1.5": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "an11.10:2.1": "“Mendicants, a mendicant with three qualities has reached the ultimate end, the ultimate sanctuary from the yoke, the ultimate spiritual life, the ultimate goal. They are best among gods and humans. ",
  "an11.10:2.2": "What three? ",
  "an11.10:2.3": "The entire spectrum of an adept’s ethics, immersion, and wisdom. ",
  "an11.10:2.4": "A mendicant with these three qualities has reached the ultimate end, the ultimate sanctuary from the yoke, the ultimate spiritual life, the ultimate goal. They are best among gods and humans. ",
  "an11.10:3.1": "A mendicant with another three qualities has reached the ultimate end, the ultimate sanctuary from the yoke, the ultimate spiritual life, the ultimate goal. They are best among gods and humans. ",
  "an11.10:3.2": "What three? ",
  "an11.10:3.3": "A demonstration of psychic power, a demonstration of revealing, and a demonstration of instruction. ",
  "an11.10:3.4": "A mendicant with these three qualities has reached the ultimate end, the ultimate sanctuary from the yoke, the